1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
ACT 1 — THE DRONE SEES: head-on intruder; det_v2 on a live camera (slow-mo x0.5)

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Step by step: detector box (conf 0.77) -> 3 consistent frames: centrality + motion

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
ADMISSION -> TRACK (judge t_acq 0.73 s); the 20-neuron liquid net takes over

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:35,300
Approach and the 6-10 m orbit — all from one 640x480 mono camera

5
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:42,300
ACT 2 — THE DRONE SEARCHES: target starts BEHIND (azimuth 180°) — empty camera

6
00:00:42,300 --> 00:00:49,300
Step-scan with the whole airframe: 40° steps, perimeter sweep

7
00:00:49,300 --> 00:01:09,400
Find, pursue, orbit — all from one 640x480 mono camera

8
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:15,400
ACT 3 — THE DRONE SURVIVES: nominal orbit; perception EMULATED in this act

9
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:21,400
We inject a GPS failure (EKF2_GPS_CTRL=0) — position starts drifting

10
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:33,300
The shield: REFUSE(POS) in ~0.1 s, then a safe D5 descent to touchdown

11
00:01:33,300 --> 00:01:40,300
ACT 4 — THE DRONE SPOTS A DECOY: the object circles, never attacks

12
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:48,300
Motion signature: fast, not closing, never below 5 m

13
00:01:48,300 --> 00:01:57,300
Rule panel (left): moving / not closing / never below 5 m — the 12-s counter grows only when ALL hold

14
00:01:57,300 --> 00:02:02,900
Label DECOY once the rule holds — the clock is shown openly

15
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:09,900
ACT 4b — THE FLAG REVERSES: the target starts out like a decoy

16
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:18,900
The classifier raises a tentative flag... but the target CHANGES behaviour

17
00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:26,900
Watch the panel: 'not closing' flips to X, then 'never below 5 m' — the label is REVOKED

18
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:37,000
Descent below 5 m => the label is REVOKED and the drone pursues

19
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:44,000
ACT 5 — INSIDE THE NETWORK: same mission as act 2; the 20-neuron state replayed deterministically

20
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Scan: the state SITS STILL. Acquisition: it JUMPS. Orbit: it circles a RING (PCA, 87.8% of variance)

21
00:02:53,000 --> 00:03:03,000
The state ring and the bearing-to-target arrow circle TOGETHER — the network remembers where the target is

22
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:15,200
Chart: neuron n0 overlaps sin(bearing) — |r|=0.96 on this take (descriptive); only T1/T2 (PROVED) on screen

23
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:23,200
ACT 6 — WIND: the same network, trained with no wind and no drag

24
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:32,200
Gusts up to 3.6 m/s, the direction swings by ±30°

25
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:50,300
The orbit holds: 6–10 m distance through the whole window

26
00:03:50,300 --> 00:03:59,300
Under wind: mild profile 8/8, sharp 7/8 — the only failure was late target recognition

27
00:03:59,300 --> 00:04:08,300
LiquidPatrol — PX4/Gazebo SITL. Zero zone breaches and zero false refusals across ~140 boots. Controller: a 20-neuron liquid network — 48/48 vs GRU 29/48 on the same grid. Decoys: recognised by behaviour — zero false alarms on attacking targets; a slow target that only circles remains indistinguishable. Controller: 20 neurons with PROVED boundedness theorems (T1/T2), activations auditable by replay. Time-varying wind up to 3.6 m/s on camera: 15/16 missions. Home hardware, evenings and weekends.
